From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] lumaShare, lumaCapture: the pill stays out of streams; Dismiss

The sharing pill, the edges and Capture's own overlays are CaptureHidden:
they skip a paint whose framebuffer is not a stage view's. A monitor
stream, though, mostly does not paint the stage: it copies what is on the
screen (a blit of the view, or of the scanout buffer), pill included, so
the pill reached the shared screen. And the screen's own paint lands in an
offscreen whenever an ancestor is redirected (an effect, an animation), so
the pill was skipped on screen for those frames and flickered.

CaptureHidden now asks the paint itself: Mutter 0036 marks every capture
paint (clutter_stage_paint_to_framebuffer and what uses it: screen casts,
screenshots) with CLUTTER_PAINT_FLAG_CAPTURE, and an on-screen paint never
carries it, whatever framebuffer it is in. While a CaptureHidden actor (or
an on-screen-only shelf surface) is mapped, it inhibits capture copies
(clutter_stage_inhibit_capture_copy), so monitor streams paint the stage
with that flag instead of copying the screen. Without the flag (an older
Mutter) the framebuffer test stays.

The pill gains Dismiss beside Stop: Stop ends the share, Dismiss puts the
pill away for the shares running now. Sharing stays visible: with the pill
away, the status cluster's sharing mark is shown, and clicking it brings
the pill back (otherwise it stops sharing, as before). A new share brings
the pill back.

